CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --replace-call-with-contract function
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[function\.precondition\.\d+\] line 1 Check requires clause of contract contract::function for function function: FAILURE$
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.1\] line 10 static array parameter .* must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
^\*\* 2 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A later compatible declaration refreshes the generated static requires clause
inside an existing code contract with the stronger minimum. The unmarked
replacement wrapper also receives the ordinary call-site precondition. The
generated assigns and frees specification functions are marked, so they add
no further failing static-array precondition.
